CORRECTION: this commit did NOT cause "no visual change".

An audit of the diff against the library CSS found three changes:

1. The Switch flipped sides. The removed .overview__switch-row was flex with
   justify-content: space-between and the text before the control, so the label sat left
   and the switch at the right edge, full width. The library Switch renders the control
   first with the copy after it at a fixed 0.75rem gap, so the control moved to the left
   of the text and the row stopped being edge-to-edge.

2. Card.Title collapsed three sizes onto one. The removed rules were 15px/600 sans,
   16px/600 and 14px/600; card__title is 14px/500 in the heading font. The dialog titles
   lost 2px and a weight step and changed family.

3. Card.Description grew. The removed rules were 13px, 13px and 12px; card__description
   is 14px.

The conversion itself was right and should stand — it is what the library owns. The
accurate claim was: "converges the page onto the library type ramp, which is the point."
